### Present ordinary Source changes immediately

**Severity:** `medium`

After the first image is displayed, assigning `Source` only stages the new value in the hidden buffer and never promotes it. Any caller that uses the dependency property directly can therefore keep showing the previous image indefinitely. Present normal `Source` updates immediately and reserve `PrepareNextImage` for coordinated staged swaps.

```suggestion
        // Ordinary Source changes should present immediately. Coordinated transitions use PrepareNextImage.
        _currentImage.Opacity = 1;
        _currentImage.Source = newSource;
        _hiddenImage.Source = null;
        _hiddenImage.Opacity = 0;
```
